//! Material Icon Theme mapping tables.
//!
//! Generated by `plans/reports/gen-icon-theme-material.py` from the
//! Material Icon Theme project (https://github.com/material-extensions/vscode-material-icon-theme),
//! commit `e355348dd69ad2b7fed0c394af54f1e80c5e36e0`.
//!
//! Source: that project's own `generateOpenFolderIcons.ts` + `generateClones.ts` +
//! `generateJson.ts` scripts were run to produce a fully-expanded VS Code icon-theme
//! manifest (`material-icons.json`), which was then converted into these tables. Only
//! icon-definition keys reachable from the base (non-opt-in) mapping tables are
//! included -- VS Code "icon pack" opt-ins (nest-*, redux-*, ngrx-*, etc.), the
//! `languageIds` table (zode has no language-id concept independent of the filename),
//! and the `light`/`highContrast` appearance overrides were all deliberately left out.
//! See `plans/reports/researcher-260822-coloured-file-icons.md` for the full rationale.
//!
//! Every file-name and file-suffix association below is lowercased, with exactly one
//! canonical spelling per association: `FileIcons::get_icon`
//! (crates/file_icons/src/file_icons.rs) lowercases the real filename before it looks
//! the result up here, matching VS Code's own case-insensitive matching. Do not add
//! UPPERCASE/Titlecase variants back in -- that lookup already covers them.
//!
//! VS Code's path-qualified associations (`.config/babelrc`, `src/bashly.yaml` and
//! 202 more) are also left out. `FileIcons::get_icon` only ever matches against
//! `Path::file_name`, so a key containing `/` cannot be reached from it -- shipping
//! them would be dead data that reads as working coverage. Every one of them has a
//! bare-filename sibling that does match.
//!
//! To regenerate: see the usage docstring at the top of
//! `plans/reports/gen-icon-theme-material.py`.

